  "description": "The general election for Pennsylvania's 14th Congressional District will be held November 3, 2026. The district covers Washington, Fayette, Greene, and portions of Westmoreland, Indiana, and Somerset counties in southwestern Pennsylvania. Incumbent Republican Guy Reschenthaler, who serves as House Chief Deputy Whip and is seeking his fifth term, faces Democratic nominee Alan Bradstock, a U.S. Army veteran and retired FBI agent, as well as American Independent Party candidate Adam Halfhill. The Cook Political Report rates the district as Solidly Republican, giving Reschenthaler a strong advantage in November.",
